  "ingredients": [
    "3 1/2 ounce rutabaga",
    "4 tablespoon coconut oil",
    "3 1/2 ounce cauliflower",
    "2 medium shallot",
    "4 tablespoon ground beef",
    "1 tablespoon celery leaves (chopped)",
    "1 tablespoon green onion (chopped)",
    "1/2 teaspoon white pepper",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1 large egg"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Slice the rutabaga into small pieces and fry in one-quarter of the coconut oil until brown.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a pestle and mortar to pound the fried rutabaga until soft. Alternately, use a food processor. Set aside once done.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Microwave the cauliflower until soft and pound, using the pestle and mortar (or food processor).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thinly slice the shallots. Using a small, shallow wok (this helps create a thicker layer of oil without actually using too much) add in another quarter of the coconut oil and fry the shallots until brown and crispy — but not burned! Set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using the same oil, sauté the ground beef until browned. Season with salt and pepper to taste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the pounded rutabaga and cauliflower, fried shallot, and cooked ground beef to a bowl. Also add in the celery leaves, green onion, white pepper (black would also work), and salt. Mix well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Scoop the mixture out in spoonfuls (about one tablespoon) and shape them into small patties.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk one egg in a separate bowl. Coat each patty lightly just before frying.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/8.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using the remaining coconut oil, fry the patties in batches until golden.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve in a stew or on their own as a snack!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/begedil-keto-potato-patties/#wprm-recipe-51539-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
